              {
                "text": "Reminders fire at the wrong time for events with a timezone offset.\n\nAn event starting at \"2026-03-10T09:00:00-05:00\" should be 14:00 UTC, but `reminder_hour_utc` (in `src/scheduling/core.py`) reports 9. Events that are already in UTC are fine. Please fix it so reminders use the correct UTC time for any offset."
              }
            ],
            "role": "user"
          },
          "final_response": {
            "parts": [
              {
                "text": "The issue was caused by `src/scheduling/parsing.py` explicitly stripping timezone information from parsed events using `.replace(tzinfo=None)`. This caused `reminder_hour_utc` in `src/scheduling/core.py` to treat all events as naive (and thus UTC), ignoring any timezone offsets provided in the input.\n\nI have removed the `.replace(tzinfo=None)` call in `src/scheduling/parsing.py`, allowing `datetime.fromisoformat` to correctly preserve the timezone information. This ensures that `to_utc` in `src/scheduling/core.py` can correctly convert the event time to UTC.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Modified `src/scheduling/parsing.py` to stop stripping timezone information.\n\n**Verification:**\n- Verified that `reminder_hour_utc` now correctly calculates 14:00 UTC for an input of `2026-03-10T09:00:00-05:00`.\n- Verified that naive timestamps (without offset) are still handled correctly as UTC.\n- Verified that UTC timestamps are handled correctly.",
